 ## Changelog
 
+- 2026-11-04 (merge of the hydro 1-3 patches and World Preview 2, written WITHOUT a Rust toolchain: not compiled, not run): `Region::water_at` (the World Preview's water) follows the new `carve`: it reads `lake_top_at`'s `(top, floor)` pair (hydro 2 changed it from a plain top), is off with `Settings::enabled`, fills a lake only over ground 40 .. top, skips a blacklisted biome (now passed in: `OverworldGenerator::water_at` reads it with `sample_at`), ground under 5, a bed under 5, a surface over 120 and ground more than 6 under the bed, like `carve`; test `the_preview_water_matches_the_carve` (not run). The settings are the global ones of the world opened last (`hydro.cfg`), so a Create World preview shows them too; the preview's generator uses `Hydro::of_preview` (its own plates, never the disk cache `cache_dir` of the world last opened: that file name holds the seed and the plate, not the type or the Natural Temperature settings).
+- 2026-11-04 (hydro 3, after `StreamsReflowing-disassembly.zip`): read `connectNetwork`, `StreamTint`, `CurrentPush`, `Lake` and the settings defaults. Ported: the mod's push factors and `current_for`, the lake shore warp, `hydro.cfg`. Corrected: `hydro::tint` (invented) removed; `connectNetwork` and `StreamTint` marked N/A with the reason. Written WITHOUT a Rust toolchain: not compiled, not run (+2 tests `a_boat_is_pushed_harder_than_a_player`, `the_lake_warp_stays_inside_four_blocks`; the settings test updated). Still open: rivers entering lakes at their level, outlet biomes / `allWaterBanks` / `riverDrainageSize`, prefetch (`StreamPrefetcher`), the 3-block Gaussian lake mask.
+- 2026-11-04 (hydro 2): bend asymmetry, hi-res lakes with a dip, the bobber in the current, flow direction on still stream tops, `hydro::tint`, the disk cache and `Settings` (written WITHOUT a Rust toolchain: not compiled, not run; +4 tests in `hydro::tests`: `a_bend_digs_its_outer_bank`, `the_cache_round_trips_and_refuses_a_cut_file`, `settings_read_their_lines`, the bed test rewritten). NOT done: `connectNetwork` (plate-border connectors: the mod's bytecode is not in the zip), rivers entering lakes at the lake's level, outlet biomes / `allWaterBanks`, prefetch, the `options.txt` wiring of `Settings`.
+- 2026-11-04 (hydro): stale notes fixed and five gaps closed in `hydro.rs` (written WITHOUT a Rust toolchain: not compiled, not run; +1 test `the_bed_is_deepest_on_the_centre_line`). Notes: the current already reached mobs, fliers and leaf / twig particles (the table said players and boats), and audio exists (the table said it did not). Code: `bed_at` (trough bed), reeds and boulders on the bank, no ice on water faster than `ICE_SPEED`, dropped items carried by the current (`Item::step`). All chosen here, UNVERIFIED against the mod. Still open: lakes' hi-res masks, `connectNetwork`, bend asymmetry, fluid block + flow rendering, bobber, per-stream tint, disk cache, biome rules, settings.
 - 2026-11-04: Natural Temperature (Caesius_Leo, Fabric 1.2.1) ported, optional per world (written WITHOUT a Rust toolchain: not compiled, not run; +4 tests: `gen::natural` x3, `menu` x1; `tools/natural_proto.py` was run against the mod's own classes: 6000 cases, 0 mismatches).
     - What it is: the temperature and humidity of the Overworld laid out in bands / rings / squares round an equator (8 modes each: default, simplified, linear, circular, banded, circular6, square6, discrete) instead of in noise blobs, so the biomes follow like the Earth's. Read from the mod's bytecode (its licence allows reverse engineering); `world/gen/natural.rs` is `MathUtils`, `TemperatureCalculator`, `HumidityCalculator` and `PainterCore`.
     - Proof: `tools/golden/NaturalHarness.java` runs the mod's own `PainterCore` on a JVM (class version patched 69 -> 65, Minecraft and Fabric stubbed, the two noises replaced by sine stubs) on random settings; `tools/natural_proto.py` (the Python twin the Rust mirrors) and the Rust test `matches_the_mods_own_classes` must give the same two numbers on `tools/golden/natural.txt` (168 cases, every mode). Mutating a constant of the twin breaks the check.
